; ====================================================================================================
; GROUND COVER (38B) - the layer this cell never had. Bare ground with four dead pines standing on it
; read as a grey box with trees in it; grass, ferns and a worn rock path are what make it a place.
;
; WARNING EVERY NODE BELOW PARENTS TO THE CELL ROOT, NOT TO Nav, AND CARRIES NO COLLIDER. That is the
; point, and it is safe in two independent ways: this cell's NavigationMesh is
; geometry_parsed_geometry_type = 1 (STATIC COLLIDERS ONLY), so a collider-less tuft could not carve
; the navmesh from inside Nav either - but parenting out states the intent where a reader will see it.
; Grass an NPC paths around is worse than no grass. The four pines above already do the same.
;
; WARNING SCALE LIVES IN THE .import, NOT HERE. The nature megakit ships its TREES at 1 m = 1 unit and
; its GROUND COVER four to ten times life size: Grass_Common_Short is 1.33 m tall in the file, clover
; 1.14 m, Flower_4_Group 2.49 m. Every prp_grass/clover/flower/fern/mushroom/pebble carries a measured
; nodes/root_scale that brings it to the size its name claims. Do not correct one in a cell transform;
; correct it in the .import so every cell gets it.
;
; WARNING GRASS GOES IN PATCHES, NOT ON A GRID. The first pass here was an even scatter of 84 props
; over 2500 sq m, and the render showed litter rather than ground cover - isolated tufts standing
; alone on bare earth look worse than nothing. These are 22 patch centres of 4-7 mixed tufts inside a
; 1.3 m radius, which is what reads as grass. Density is the thing to judge, not count, and only a
; render at eye level shows it.
;
; WARNING THE SHADE SPECIES CLEAR THE TRUNK, NOT THE CANOPY. Ferns and mushrooms are clustered under
; the pines on purpose. The first pass applied every feature's full keep-out radius to them too and
; placed 2 ferns and 0 mushrooms - the exclusion silently deleted the thing it was placing. They now
; use 22% of each radius, which clears the trunk and nothing else; the pines have no collider, so
; there is nothing else to clear.
;
; Positions are a seeded scatter (tools/gen_cell_props.py, seed 38) that keeps clear of the pines,
; rocks, ruins, crate and all four pickups, and leaves a 1.5 m gap either side of the path.
;
; ponytail: one Node3D per tuft, because the .tscn stays the authored, greppable artefact the
; generator's docstring defends. If ground cover reaches every cell and the node count starts to
; cost, the upgrade is a MultiMeshInstance3D per species with the mesh extracted through the
; importer's _subresources save_to_file - one node and one draw call instead of ~150.
; ====================================================================================================

[node name="Path1" type="Node3D" parent="."]
